  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Clicking and stopping",
      "items": [
        "The app passes click settings or macro events to daemon worker threads; clicking the main button or the configured hotkey toggles or stops the run. (autoclicker/app.py:42–60, 63–105)",
        "Fixed click mode ends at its count. A non-positive click interval is raised to 50 ms; optional interval jitter and multi-point targets are applied in the worker. (autoclicker/app.py:85–103; autoclicker/engine.py:18–55)",
        "Workers update the counter and schedule status refreshes back onto the Tk app. A click-loop input exception stops that loop and clears the running flag. (autoclicker/app.py:14–20; autoclicker/engine.py:42–55)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Recording and replay",
      "items": [
        "Recording stores pressed mouse buttons with elapsed time and screen coordinates, plus keyboard presses; the capture callbacks do not record pointer-only movement events. (autoclicker/app.py:141–191)",
        "Replay waits between recorded event times, clicks at captured coordinates, and presses recorded keys; replay can be finite or infinite. (autoclicker/app.py:679–698; autoclicker/engine.py:58–82)",
        "PyAutoGUI's top-left failsafe is enabled. The click loop stops on an input exception, while macro replay catches per-event exceptions and continues to later events. (autoclicker/dependencies.py:16–20; autoclicker/engine.py:42–55, 71–82)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Persistence and privacy",
      "items": [
        "Settings load from ~/.autoclicker_config.json at startup and save on request or close. Invalid or unreadable settings are silently ignored. (autoclicker/config.py:3–5; autoclicker/app.py:265–310, 819–830)",
        "Macro save and open dialogs use a user-selected JSON path. Files can contain key presses and screen coordinates, so review them before sharing. (autoclicker/app.py:211–235; README.md:40–42)",
        "The app does not itself grant system input access: macOS Accessibility permissions may be needed, and other platforms depend on their permission and input-library support. (README.md:28)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Packaging and checks",
      "items": [
        "The local build helper installs PyInstaller if needed, deletes prior build/ and dist/ folders and root .spec files, then produces a one-file executable for the current OS. (build.py:25–64)",
        "Engine tests replace PyAutoGUI with a mock and patch sleeps; they test counts, multipoint clicks, errors and replay without real input events. (tests/test_engine.py:1–68)",
        "The GitHub workflow runs Pylint on Python 3.8, 3.9 and 3.10; it does not run the unit-test command. (.github/workflows/pylint.yml:5–23; README.md:55–63)"
      ]
    }
  ]
